                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Can't get past one section as it's timed, and the timer starts running while the dialogue box is up. Thought this game was going to chill me out, but it's actually quite stressful - I've played horror games that I find calmer! Wish there was an option to skip puzzles.\n\n The game looks stunning, but if I can't actually play it the beautiful looks are worthless. Having no jump button is also a wee bit of a headscratcher, as well is being unable to close certain windows by clicking the close button.\n\ni also don't really feel like I'm actually part of the world - I can't interact with much and, as such, I don't really feel immersed or that my character actually exists within a place. As such there's always a feeling of detachment even if I'm enjoying the exploration.",
